\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} &= \frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} \\ &= \frac{x^{2^n}}{x^{2(2^n)} - x^{-2(2^n)}}
\end{align*}
We can then regroup the quotient as follows:
\[\frac{x^{2^n}}{-2x^{2(2^n)} + x^{2(2^n)}} \cdot x^{2(2^n)}\]
Since $x^{2(2^n)}$ is in the form $y^2 - 1$, we have that:
\[\frac{x^{2^n}}{y^2 - 1} \cdot y^2\]
Taking the reciprocal of both sides gives us:
\begin{align*}
\frac{1}{y^2 - 1} &= \frac{1}{x^{2^n}} \cdot \frac{1}{y^2} \\
(x^{2^n})^{-1}(x^{2(2^n)})^2 &= 1 \\
\sum_{n = 0}^\infty \frac{1}{x^{2^n} - x^{-2^n}} &= \boxed{1}.
\end{align*} The answer is: 1
